ove is likely a **small to moderate raise** (e.g., 100) or slightly higher, but since 100 is the minimum allowed raise and within safe bounds, it serves well as a **semi-bluff** — representing strength while having solid backup equity.\n\nReason:  \nRaising by 100 is optimal because:\n- It protects your hand by charging opponents who may be drawing to better hands.\n- It continues aggression from pre-flop and flop, maintaining image of strength.\n- It avoids over-committing with a draw, yet builds the pot for when you hit.\n- Opponent has shown passivity (checking/calling); they’re likely to fold marginal hands, giving you fold equity.\n- A tiny raise keeps you in control and doesn’t scare off worse hands completely.\n\nAnswer: 100"}
